[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
| Requirement group | Primary tests |
| --- | --- |
| SWR-ROUTINE-* | `test_safety_routines.py`, `test_safetyFunctions.py`, `test_localization.py`, frontend `safetyRoutines.test.ts` and `safety-routines.spec.ts` |
| SWR-CFG-* | `test_app_cfg_validator.py`, `test_component_schema_validation.py` |
| SWR-SM-* | shared lifecycle and execution contract tests across all six component families: repeated start/stop, explicit input binding, metadata-only changes, disabled/obsolete callback rejection, owned handle cancellation and domain timing preservation |
| SWR-TEMP-* | `test_temperatureComponent.py`, `test_derivative_monitor.py`, `test_safetyFunctions.py` |
| SWR-DOOR-* | `test_safety_doors_component.py`, `test_app_cfg_validator.py` |
| SWR-FLT-* | `test_fault_manager.py`, `test_fault_evidence.py`, `test_degradation.py`, `test_self_diagnostics.py`, `test_system_notification_recovery.py` |
| SWR-NOT-* | `test_notify_man.py`, `test_notification_history.py`, `test_safetyhome_api_gateway.py`, `test_notification_schema.py`, `test_notification_state_store.py`, `test_system_notification_recovery.py`, frontend notification-history domain and component tests |
| SWR-REC-* | `test_recovery_man.py`, `test_recovery_manual_contract.py`, `test_recovery_allocations.py`, `test_recovery_state_store.py`, `test_system_notification_recovery.py`; component action-allocation tests, authenticated manual-report contract tests, frontend action/fault/completion tests and localization tests shall cover the shared recovery contract |
| SWR-LOC-* | `test_localization.py`, `test_mqtt_entity_manager.py`, frontend domain tests |
| SWR-MQTT-* | `test_mqtt_entity_manager.py`, `test_safetyFunctions.py` |
| SWR-EXT-* | provider contract tests, external hazard policy tests, EventBus/FaultManager/notification integration tests, full startup/test-dispatch/preview/shutdown with the German dummy, explicit target-model and obsolete-shape rejection tests, synthetic isolation from real H/D/degradation/coverage/actions, metadata-driven frontend provider-or-disabled/parameter/country tests, same-start applied truth and muted disabled presentation, localization parity, negative-actuation tests |
| SWR-ENT-* | entity health registry/check/state-machine tests, component dependency and common-entity integration tests, FaultManager/MQTT tests, frontend monitored-list/filter and route tests, negative-actuation tests |
| SWR-FSM-* | source contract and unit/freshness tests, memory/PSI and disk/thermal qualification and recovery tests, WAN/update/battery/backup policy tests, durable operational-test attestation tests, fault-owner deduplication, independent-watchdog evidence, and negative-actuation tests |
| SWR-HSM-* | normalized telemetry/code-profile tests, independent-need and phase tests, thermal/distribution/counter rules, timing/restart/clock tests, C-ENT/FaultManager integration, SET/HEAL correlation, frontend diagnostics/localization and negative-actuation tests; detailed mapping in the Heating System Monitoring architecture |
| SWR-IEHM-* | detector/profile fixtures, binary alarm edge/latch tests, PM unit/window/coverage tests, health ownership, timing/restart/corruption tests, hazard-specific output/advice conflicts, incident/journal/UI/localization and negative-actuation tests; detailed mapping in the Internal Environmental Hazard Monitoring architecture |
| SWR-LEAK-* | water-leak profile/configuration tests, independent latch and positive-clear tests, unavailable-source hold, L2 fault configuration, periodic test inventory, frontend leak-state display and negative-actuation tests |
| SWR-NFR-005 | pytest-cov application-code report |
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SSRD-SEC-8
TITLE: Assurance boundary

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SafetyComponent provides monitoring and response assistance within a Home
Assistant installation. Home Assistant, AppDaemon, the host, networks, sensors,
actuators, cloud providers, and notification transports are external or
non-certified dependencies. This software and its documentation do not claim
regulatory certification, guaranteed provider availability, or medical guidance.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SSRD-SEC-9
TITLE: Change control

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Changes to raw state codes, entity-ID generation, fault severity mapping,
timing semantics, notification correlation, recovery service allow-lists, or
configuration validation are safety-contract changes. They require an SSRD
update, regression tests, review, and controlled deployment verification.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
